  "tagline": "Postgres vector extension built on USearch HNSW; development has stalled since late 2024.",
  "description": "Lantern is a PostgreSQL extension from the YC-backed Lantern Systems that adds a lantern_hnsw index type based on USearch, with faster external index builds, in-database embedding generation and BM25 text search through its lantern_extras companion. It was pitched as a quicker alternative to pgvector's HNSW. Since v0.5.0 in November 2024 there have been no releases and the repository has had no commits since December 2024, while pgvector closed most of the performance gap. Lantern Cloud's website is still online, but the project looks dormant; prefer pgvector, VectorChord or pgvectorscale for new work.",
